Reddit users have helped identify missing or unidentified individuals, clarify evidence in criminal cases, and spot non-crime hazards behind mysteries. [1] (https://www.cbc.ca/shortdocs/features/reddit-websleuths), [2] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=um5qPGy9iAU)
• Grateful Doe (Jason Callahan) (https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=%2Fg%2F11bylhyfbb&q=real+crime+cases+that+were+solved+on+reddit+grateful+doe+%28jason+callahan%29): A young man killed in a 1995 car crash in Virginia remained unidentified for 20 years until Reddit users on r/UnresolvedMysteries connected clues—such as Grateful Dead lyrics found in his pocket—to a missing person report, later confirmed via DNA. [1] (https://www.cbc.ca/shortdocs/features/reddit-websleuths), [2] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=um5qPGy9iAU)
• Linda Marie Pagano (https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=%2Fg%2F11f0tm7f5w&q=real+crime+cases+that+were+solved+on+reddit+linda+marie+pagano): Skeletal remains found in Ohio in 1975 were linked to a 1974 missing person report after a student shared cemetery records on Reddit and a volunteer forensic artist created a reconstruction; DNA testing later confirmed her identity, leading police to reopen the homicide case. [1] (https://medium.com/@divyagupta_62030/how-reddit-solved-a-40-year-cold-case-and-why-i-havent-stopped-thinking-about-it-4b03156bd64e), [2] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piycfL5aBcs)
• Lyle Stevik (https://www.google.com/search?kgmid=%2Fm%2F012hy_n9&q=real+crime+cases+that+were+solved+on+reddit+lyle+stevik): An unidentified man who died by suicide in Washington state in 2001 was eventually identified through genetic genealogy after Reddit users helped crowdfund DNA testing. [1] (https://www.reddit.com/r/UnresolvedMysteries/comments/cjwh2r/any_formerly_unresolved_mysteries_that_were/)
• Hit-and-run vehicle identification: Online sleuths on Reddit helped identify the make and model of a suspect's car from a broken vehicle fragment left at a hit-and-run scene, aiding law enforcement. [1] (https://www.cbc.ca/shortdocs/features/reddit-websleuths), [2] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=um5qPGy9iAU)
• Walter Scott shooting video analysis: A Redditor enhanced and stabilized raw bystander footage of the 2015 police shooting in South Carolina, helping clarify what happened on camera. [1] (https://www.cbc.ca/shortdocs/features/reddit-websleuths)
• Mysterious Post-it notes: In a well-known non-crime thread, Redditors suggested a carbon monoxide leak after a user found unexplained notes around his apartment—a warning that turned out to be accurate and potentially life-saving. [1] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=um5qPGy9iAU)
Reddit investigations also have a mixed track record—most notably during the 2013 Boston Marathon bombing manhunt, where online speculation misidentified innocent people. [1] (https://www.cbc.ca/shortdocs/features/reddit-websleuths)
